questions.stem:
A bakery ledger claims a tail-recursive total but prints 24 for a run that must total 10.
static int tally(int n, int acc) { if (n == 0) return acc; return tally(n - 1, acc * n); }
System.out.println(tally(4, 1));
What is printed, and why?

An auditor's digit total prints 7 for the number 47. The method is:
static int digitSum(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return n % 10 + digitSum(n / 100); }
Which replacement for the divisor makes it correct?

A number-theory club's helper hangs when asked for gcd(2, 9):
static int gcd(int a, int b) { if (b == 0) return a; return gcd(a, b - a); }
What actually happens, and why?

A census tool reports 2 even values for {1, 2, 4, 6}, but 3 of them are even. The method is:
static int countEven(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length - 1) return 0; int k = a[i] % 2 == 0 ? 1 : 0; return k + countEven(a, i + 1); }
Which repair is correct?

A club accepts a submission only if the method terminates and returns the right value. Which of these four are correctly written recursive methods? Select all that apply.
A. static int s(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return n + s(n - 1); }
B. static int t(int n) { return n + t(n - 1); }
C. static int u(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return u(n); }
D. static int v(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return n + v(n - 2); }

A counting monitor tallies every invocation, the first one included, for this method:
public static int ways(int n) { if (n <= 1) return 1; return ways(n - 1) + ways(n - 2); }
How many ways invocations run while evaluating ways(4)?

A profiler records the deepest activation reached while running:
public static int halve(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return 1 + halve(n / 2); }
How many halve frames are live on the stack at that moment for halve(1000)?

A choir cues each syllable with an opening and a closing marker:
public static void box(String s) { if (s.isEmpty()) return; System.out.print("<" + s.charAt(0)); box(s.substring(1)); System.out.print(s.charAt(0) + ">"); }
Calling box("ab") prints one line. What is printed?

A tally board doubles each bin once every bin has been visited:
public static void mark(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return; mark(a, i + 1); a[i] = a[i] * 2; }
int[] a = {1, 2, 3};
mark(a, 0);
What does a hold afterwards?

A parity checker is instrumented so that every invocation increments a counter:
public static int pick(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; if (n % 2 == 0) return pick(n / 2); return 1 + pick(n - 1); }
Counting every invocation including the first, how many run for pick(13)?

A stepper doubles the answer from each level:
public static int pair(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return 2 * pair(n / 2) + 1; }
What integer does pair(12) return?

A formatter wraps every level of a count in brackets:
public static String nest(int n) { if (n == 0) return ""; return "[" + n + nest(n - 1) + "]"; }
System.out.println(nest(3));
What line is printed?

An inspector freezes the debugger at the instant the final frame is entered while this runs:
public static int ways(int n) { if (n <= 1) return 1; return ways(n - 1) + ways(n - 2); }
How many ways frames are on the stack at that instant for ways(4)?

A branching helper is instrumented for a small input:
public static int spread(int n) { if (n == 0) return 1; return spread(n - 1) + spread(n - 1) + spread(n - 1); }
A monitor records the call tree of spread(2). Which statements about that tree are true? Select all that apply.

A total is requested from an index the caller never validated:
public static int sumFrom(int[] a, int i) { if (i >= a.length) return 0; return a[i] + sumFrom(a, i + 1); }
int[] a = {5, 7};
System.out.println(sumFrom(a, -1));
What happens?

Every invocation of this method, the first one included, is tallied:
public static int spread(int n) { if (n == 0) return 1; return spread(n - 1) + spread(n - 1) + spread(n - 1); }
How many invocations run in total for spread(3)?

A firmware trace prints remainders from the bottom up:
public static void show(int n) { if (n == 0) return; System.out.print(n % 2); show(n / 2); }
show(13);
What is printed?

A lister builds its output by string concatenation:
public static String show(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return ""; return a[i] + " " + show(a, i + 1); }
System.out.print(show(new int[]{2, 5, 7}, 0));
What is printed?

A bit counter is instrumented to count every invocation, the first included:
public static int countBits(int n) { if (n == 0) return 0; return n % 2 + countBits(n / 2); }
How many invocations run for countBits(100)?

A weaver alternates characters from two strings and recurses twice per call:
public static void weave(String a, String b) { if (a.isEmpty()) { System.out.print(b); return; } if (b.isEmpty()) { System.out.print(a); return; } System.out.print(a.charAt(0)); weave(a.substring(1), b); System.out.print(b.charAt(0)); weave(a, b.substring(1)); }
weave("ab", "12");
What is printed?
